1. T2 degree-reversibility equivalence and higher-arity generalization.
2. T4 complement-filtration correspondence.
3. T3 logical reversal / cyclic inversion semantic bridge.
4. T8 complete chain-ring contextuality classification.
5. T9 uniform nilpotent Hardy family.
6. T11 even-dimensional binary-orthogonal operator-basis obstruction.
7. T15 same unrestricted rank but different restricted contextuality.

The broad conceptual research object is the restricted modal/operator theory obtained by starting from a four-cycle on the coefficient positions of a binary Boolean function, taking its rotation-equivariant algebra, and restricting multipartite transformations and measurements to structures inherited from that algebra.
